From: Fabric Production Readiness Agent <agent@fabric.dev>
Date: 2026-01-15
Subject: [PATCH 008] Hardcoded Demo Data Guard (P0)

Problem:
- ProspectPromptBuilder.tsx imports DEFAULT_COMPANIES and DEFAULT_ACTIVITIES
  directly from @/lib/demoData without a DEV guard.
- While demoData.ts has internal gating, the import itself should be gated
  to prevent any accidental inclusion of customer names in production bundles.
- No CI enforcement exists to prevent real customer names from leaking into
  production component code.

Solution:
1. Extract dev-only demo fixtures to apps/web/src/test/fixtures/demo-prospects.ts
   with clear DEV-only markings.
2. Update demoData.ts to import from the new fixtures location.
3. Gate the demo data import in ProspectPromptBuilder.tsx behind
   import.meta.env.DEV so it only loads in development builds.
4. Add CI script scripts/security/assert-no-demo-data-in-production.mjs that
   scans dist/public for known customer names and fails the build if found.
5. Update CI workflow to run the new security gate.

Files changed:
- apps/web/src/test/fixtures/demo-prospects.ts (new)
- apps/web/src/lib/demoData.ts (update import source)
- apps/web/src/components/workspace/ProspectPromptBuilder.tsx (DEV-gated import)
- apps/web/scripts/security/assert-no-demo-data-in-production.mjs (new)
